[h1]SaucedCarts v2.1.17[/h1]

[b]Fixed: on dedicated servers, we were damaging your sandbox settings file on every startup.[/b]
Three server admins reported the same thing on 42.20.1, and this one is entirely ours. <server>_SandboxVars.lua was being cut short on each boot, and because the leftover file is incomplete the server would fail to read it on the restart after that — coming up with no sandbox configuration until someone restored the file by hand. It affected the settings for every mod on the server, not just ours, and to make it worse our own log line said the operation had succeeded. We're sorry; that's a bad way to spend an evening and several of you did.

The feature behind it had a real purpose. A dedicated server writes that settings file before mods have registered their translations, so every mod's options land in it bare — no explanatory comment, no "1 = Off, 2 = Rare" value map — leaving you editing blind. Since v2.1.13 we loaded the translations after startup and asked the game to write the file again, filling all of that back in for every mod you had installed.

What changed is that the latest patch made the game run all text through its formatter. A single option description containing a stray percent sign now raises an error, and the game's writer empties the file before it starts writing and doesn't guard against that error. The write stops dead part-way through, and what has been written so far is all that survives. One mod anywhere on the server with a mistyped description was enough.

[b]We removed the rewrite entirely rather than trying to make it safe.[/b] We did try. We tested every description up front to catch a bad one before writing — on a real 42.20.1 server that check passes and the file still gets cut, because the failure doesn't surface to us the way it does inside the game. We can't repair the file afterwards either, since the game no longer permits mods to write .lua files at all, which also rules out writing to a temporary file and swapping it in. Only rewriting "when the comments are missing" doesn't help, because on a dedicated server they're missing every single boot.

That left a straightforward choice: helpful comments in a config file, against the risk of destroying every mod's settings on your server on every restart, through a part of the game we don't control and can't guard. We'll take neither. The file is now left completely alone.

We kept the harmless half — the mod still refreshes translations after startup, which writes nothing and helps other mods resolve their text on the server. If the comments turn out to be genuinely missed, we can publish them as a separate reference file that sits alongside your save and never touches your configuration. Tell us if that's worth having.

[b]If your file is already truncated:[/b] start the server once with SaucedCarts disabled. The game writes a complete file on its own at boot and your settings will come back. Then update and re-enable.

[b]Also worth knowing:[/b] the underlying trigger is a mod translation with an unescaped percent sign, and it isn't specific to us. If you're seeing other odd errors since 42.20.1, that's a likely cause — since that patch a literal percent has to be written twice over in translation files.

[b]And some good news:[/b] the build 42.20.2 that just went out fixes that trigger on the game's side — it now catches the error instead of letting it escape, so a mod with a stray percent sign will log a warning rather than break things around it. Updating your server is worth doing regardless of this mod. We're still removing our rewrite, because servers on 42.20.0 and 42.20.1 are still exposed and because the part of the game that empties the file before writing it is unchanged — it just has one fewer way to go wrong.

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Save-safe.[/b] No save or database changes, no settings migration. Safe to apply mid-run.
[/list]
